{"schema_version":"benchmark-q1-semantic-issue-coverage-judgment-luna5","question_id":"Q1-semantic-issue-coverage","status":"ok","judge_run_name":"luna8-api-v4-medium-mimo-v26pro-rl-max-full200-n04","prediction_set_name":"mimo-v26pro-rl-max-full200-n04","paper_id":"2511.02700","judge_input_sha256":"96df6ef441c8670a95f7ccfb46a5cd533ff425e080fbb93ac5fba7f4ca144b73","gold_decisions":[{"gold_issue_id":"2511.02700:I001","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2511.02700:I001:U001","2511.02700:I001:U002","2511.02700:I001:U003","2511.02700:I001:U004","2511.02700:I001:U006","2511.02700:I001:U007","2511.02700:I001:U008"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U006","ISSUE-001:U010"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue concerns an unsupported second-order convergence claim for the entire numerical scheme versus a narrower quadrature estimate. ISSUE-001 instead concerns moment criteria and the necessity of a Levy-measure tail condition; it does not diagnose the missing full-scheme consistency, stability, and convergence argument.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2511.02700:I002","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-001","focus_relation":"different_causal_subject","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2511.02700:I002:U001","2511.02700:I002:U002","2511.02700:I002:U003","2511.02700:I002:U004","2511.02700:I002:U005","2511.02700:I002:U007"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-001:U001","ISSUE-001:U003","ISSUE-001:U010"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue identifies the missing density-variation or derivative hypothesis needed for the weighted midpoint quadrature estimate. ISSUE-001 addresses directional versus norm-based exponential moment conditions and does not recognize the quadrature regularity obligation or its failure for rough densities.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2511.02700:I004","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-002","focus_relation":"different_obligation_or_hypothesis","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2511.02700:I004:U001","2511.02700:I004:U002","2511.02700:I004:U003","2511.02700:I004:U004","2511.02700:I004:U005","2511.02700:I004:U007","2511.02700:I004:U008"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-002:U001","ISSUE-002:U003","ISSUE-002:U009"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is that allowing singular positive-semidefinite rho makes inverse- and determinant-based NTS density formulas undefined, requiring a positive-definite hypothesis. ISSUE-002 diagnoses a wrong lambda factor in the NTS variance formula and does not address the admissible matrix hypothesis or well-definedness of the density formulas.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]}],"audit":{"all_gold_ids_decided":true,"all_ranked_candidates_considered":true,"target_type_not_used_for_identity":true,"severity_not_used_for_identity":true,"prediction_reuse_requires_explicit_issue_support":true,"each_gold_credited_at_most_once":true,"combined_entries_are_self_contained_diagnoses":true,"support_limit_three_respected":true}}